[js/packages/store/chat/index.ts] I'm not sure I understand your reply

If you don't make this change in the `protocol` orchestrator too: the `instance` orchestrator is never ran and so, when dispatching `instance.start`, the `console.warn` shown below is not executed
```js
// instance.ts
takeEvery(commands.start, function*() {
    // TODO: do protocol things
    console.warn("HELLO SAGA")
    yield put(events.started())
}),
```
In other words: even if the `protocol.orchestrator` is run directly with `sagaMiddleware.run` we need to add a `call` like shown below
```js
// protocol/index.ts
export function* orchestrator() {
    yield all([
        call(instance.orchestrator)
    ])
}
```

